### Building Comfort — HTTP requests
#
# Ready-made requests for the app's control endpoints. In VS Code, install the
# "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client) and click "Send Request" above any
# request. The app must be running (npm run demo).

@host = http://localhost:3000

### List all rooms with their current readings
GET {{host}}/api/rooms

### Break a room (too hot / dry / high CO2)
POST {{host}}/api/rooms/room_01_01_01
Content-Type: application/json

{ "temperature": 40, "humidity": 20, "co2": 700 }

### Set custom readings for a room
POST {{host}}/api/rooms/room_01_02_03
Content-Type: application/json

{ "temperature": 82, "humidity": 40, "co2": 10 }

### Reset a single room to comfortable defaults
POST {{host}}/api/rooms/room_01_01_01/reset

### Reset every room
POST {{host}}/api/reset

### Turn the simulator on
POST {{host}}/api/simulate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "enabled": true }

### Turn the simulator off
POST {{host}}/api/simulate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "enabled": false }

### Subscribe to the live snapshot stream (Server-Sent Events)
GET {{host}}/events
Accept: text/event-stream
